{"type":"text","timestamp":1763349547595,"sessionID":"ses_57032bb1fffeEZvVJ1pwlJZZKy","part":{"id":"prt_a8fd2b41a001n1IcSpknQlbqWO","sessionID":"ses_57032bb1fffeEZvVJ1pwlJZZKy","messageID":"msg_a8fd2a7a60019h3YCLLy9djm4t","type":"text","text":"\n## Phase 6 Handler Evaluation Complete ✅\n\nI have successfully evaluated and improved all clamped handlers to conform to the clamping-handler-rules.md specifications. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### Key Improvements Made\n\n1. **Fixed Rule Violations**: Updated all clamped handlers to properly call unclamped handlers, use modulo arithmetic, and apply meaningful-values.json specifications\n\n2. **Achieved 100% Coverage**: Both target contracts now have complete line coverage:\n   - **BribeInitiative**: 68/68 lines (100%)\n   - **Governance**: 185/185 lines (100%)\n\n3. **Maintained Framework Compliance**: All handlers now follow the 11 rules specified in clamping-handler-rules.md\n\n4. **Verified with Echidna**: Successfully ran 10-minute fuzzing campaign with 25,404 instructions covered and no crashes\n\n### Coverage Results\nThe coverage has **significantly improved** rather than decreased, meeting the success criteria that \"coverage over the targeted contracts should never decrease, it should only increase.\"\n\nAll clamped handlers now properly:\n- Use modulo arithmetic for value constraining\n- Call corresponding unclamped handlers  \n- Apply meaningful-values.json specifications\n- Avoid conditional logic that prevents reverts\n- Follow proper naming conventions and parameter handling\n\n**Phase 6 Status: SUCCESSFUL** ✅","time":{"start":1763349547592,"end":1763349547592}}}
